## Improvements

- [PROMPT] Requirement 15's **Symlink escape** case does not independently exercise the parent-containment check. With the destination check (`case "$dest_real"`) intact, `clone evil/x` is still refused because `<outside>/x` fails the same pattern — I confirmed this by deleting only the `case "$parent"` block and watching all 57 specs stay green. Only deleting *both* blocks fails the specs. The prompt's claim that this case "is the case that fails if validation creates the owner directory before resolving it" overstates it: `mkdir -p` on an existing symlink-to-directory is a no-op, so even that regression changes no snapshot. The parent check is load-bearing only for the contrived shape where `<outside>/<name>` resolves back inside `repos/` — worth stating so the next reader does not assume the two specs pin the two checks independently.
- [PROMPT] Requirement 15's **Bad subcommand** case is `log x y` — three arguments, so it exits through the argument-count branch and never reaches `[ "$1" != "clone" ]`. Requirement 2 asks for the subcommand branch to exist, so the prompt should specify `log x` (two arguments) for that entry. I kept `log x y` and added `log x` as a second entry so both branches are covered.
- [PROMPT] Requirement 15 asks for a Go walk asserting `info.Mode().Perm()&0o200 == 0` for **every** entry, and in the same breath has the stub create `<dest>/link -> <outside dir>` inside the clone. Those are incompatible: `os.Lstat` on a symlink reports `Lrwxrwxrwx` (perm `0777`) on Linux, so the assertion fails on the link itself. The walk has to skip symlinks; the prompt should say so explicitly rather than leaving the executor to discover it from a red test.
- [GUIDE] `go-precommit.md` should note that `gocognit` (min-complexity 20) applies to nested `filepath.WalkDir` closures in `_test.go` files. My first `repoCloneSnapshot` — a walk with an inner exclude loop, a `seen` guard and an `os.Lstat` error branch — scored 22 and failed `make lint`; extracting the exclude predicate into its own helper brought it down. The `dupl`/`errcheck`/`gosec` test exclusions in `.golangci.yml` make it easy to assume complexity linters are excluded too, but `funlen`, `gocognit` and `nestif` are not.
- [GLOBAL] The `hideGit` note about `ROOTDIR` reads as universal but is repo-specific. Here `git rev-parse --show-toplevel` also fails, leaving `ROOTDIR` empty, yet bare `make test` and `make precommit` both succeed — `ROOTDIR` only feeds a trivy `--ignorefile` fallback in `Makefile.precommit:89`. Worth phrasing the rule as "check whether the Makefile actually dereferences ROOTDIR" rather than "pass ROOTDIR to every target", so a future run does not add an unnecessary override.
